      "summaries": {
        "en": "Orca is an Agent Development Environment (ADE) that orchestrates multiple AI coding agents in parallel, solving the bottleneck of single-agent workflows. Its core innovation is agent-fleet parallelism: each agent operates independently on different tasks, coordinated through a unified interface, dramatically boosting productivity. Users bring their own API subscriptions, run agents like Claude Code or Cursor Agent, and extend via plugins. Ideal for complex code reviews, refactoring, or cross-checking solutions across multiple agents simultaneously.",
        "zh": "Orca是一种智能体开发环境（ADE），专门用于并行运行多个AI编程智能体。它解决了单智能体协作效率低下的问题，核心创新在于智能体舰队式并行：每个代理独立处理不同任务，通过统一界面协调工作，大幅提升开发效率。用户可使用自有订阅运行Claude Code、Cursor Agent等代理，并支持插件扩展。适用于复杂代码审查、重构、多方案并行验证等场景，让开发者同时调用多个智能体协同作战，快速迭代代码。",
        "es": "Orca is an Agent Development Environment (ADE) that orchestrates multiple AI coding agents in parallel, solving the bottleneck of single-agent workflows. Its core innovation is agent-fleet parallelism: each agent operates independently on different tasks, coordinated through a unified interface, dramatically boosting productivity. Users bring their own API subscriptions, run agents like Claude Code or Cursor Agent, and extend via plugins. Ideal for complex code reviews, refactoring, or cross-checking solutions across multiple agents simultaneously.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "orca stands out for ade, agent-ide, and ai-agents in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Orca is an Agent Development Environment (ADE) that orchestrates multiple AI coding agents in parallel, solving the bottleneck of single-agent workflows. Its core innovation is agent-fleet parallelism: each agent operates independently on different tasks, coordinated through a unified interface, dramatically boosting productivity. Users bring their own API subscriptions, run agents like Claude Code or Cursor Agent, and extend via plugins. Ideal for complex code reviews, refactoring, or cross-checking solutions across multiple agents simultaneously.",
